<hr/><p>08.10.2026 09:07 Political News</p><h3>Russia escalates to sabotage against Danish weapons manufacturers supplying Ukraine – intelligence – Reuters</h3><p class=MsoNormal>KYIV. Oct 8 (Interfax-Ukraine) – The Russian Federation has launched sabotage operations against Danish companies supplying defense products to Ukraine after previous destabilization attempts failed to weaken Western military support for Kyiv, Chief Analyst of the Danish Security and Intelligence Service (PET) Josefine Christensen stated at a domestic security conference in Copenhagen on Wednesday, Reuters reports.</p>
<p class=MsoNormal>According to her, this marks a significant escalation of hybrid warfare by Moscow.</p>
<p class=MsoNormal>"In the spring, we saw a lot of planning, but very little was put into practice; at the beginning of the summer, we saw that they started moving much more into implementation," Christensen noted, emphasizing that previous wide-scale attacks "had no effect in deterring the Western NATO block from supporting Ukraine."</p>
<p class=MsoNormal>The Danish intelligence representative stressed that Moscow maintains political control over these operations, yet their boldness is growing: Russia "is trying to hit targets that have a direct impact on the front line, i.e., weapons production." Christensen also recalled a "list" published in April by the Russian Ministry of Defense targeting a number of European UAV manufacturers and component suppliers, which Moscow designated as potential military targets.</p>
<p class=MsoNormal>According to Danish intelligence, to carry out sabotage operations, Russian handlers are increasingly recruiting untrained perpetrators, particularly via Telegram and social media, offering "quick money." Typically, recruitment begins with simpler tasks, such as reconnaissance or photographing facilities, before escalating into actual acts of sabotage.</p>
<p class=MsoNormal>The Russian Embassy in Copenhagen traditionally rejected the accusations, calling them groundless.</p>
