<hr/><p>08.10.2026 10:20 Political News</p><h3>Two teenagers killed, 6 injured in Russian attacks, ordnance detonation in Sumy region – National Police</h3><p class=MsoNormal>KYIV. Oct 8 (Interfax-Ukraine) – Two minors were killed and another six people sustained injuries and trauma as a result of Russian strikes and the detonation of an explosive object in Sumy region, the National Police of Ukraine reported on its Telegram channel on Thursday.</p>
<p class=MsoNormal>"Over the past 24 hours, Russia attacked 26 settlements in the region. In the Krolevets community, two 14-year-old boys were killed as a result of the detonation of an explosive object," the statement reads.</p>
<p class=MsoNormal>In addition, three people were injured in the Sumy community due to a UAV strike, while two other women sought medical assistance following an attack on October 6. In the Velyka Pysarivka community, a 62-year-old man was wounded by Russian drone strike.</p>
<p class=MsoNormal>According to law enforcement, residential buildings, vehicles, and energy and civil infrastructure facilities suffered damage. Police investigators are documenting the aftermath of war crimes and establishing all the circumstances of the tragedy.</p>
<p class=MsoNormal>As reported, on Wednesday evening, Head of the Sumy Regional Military Administration Oleh Hryhorov stated that two 14-year-old boys in the Konotop district had encountered an unknown explosive object in a field, which detonated, causing the teenagers to die on the spot.</p>
