<hr/><p>08.10.2026 11:14 Business News</p><h3>Winter grain sowing in Ukraine reaches nearly 50% of target</h3><p class=MsoNormal>KYIV. Oct 8 (Interfax-Ukraine) – As of October 7, Ukrainian farmers had sown 2.52 million hectares with winter grain crops, or 48.4% of the projected area, and 1.041 million hectares with winter rapeseed, or 94.2% of the forecast, the Ministry of Agrarian Policy and Food reported on its website Wednesday.</p>
<p class=MsoNormal>In particular, wheat and triticale (a hybrid of wheat and rye) had been sown on 2.253 million hectares (49.6% of the forecast), barley on 209,900 hectares (35.4%), and rye on 57,800 hectares (75.3%).</p>
<p class=MsoNormal>Over the past week, the area sown with grain crops increased by 925,700 hectares, compared with an increase of 853,200 hectares the previous week.</p>
<p class=MsoNormal>Last year, by this date, 2.572 million hectares had been sown with grain crops, just 2% more than this year. The area sown with wheat was 4.2% larger, while barley and rye sowings were larger this year, by 17.1% and 26.5%, respectively.</p>
<p class=MsoNormal>As for rapeseed, its sowing season is nearing completion: over the past week, the area increased by just 22,900 hectares, compared with 59,200 hectares the previous week. This year's rapeseed sowings as of this date are 5.6% larger than last year's.</p>
<p class=MsoNormal>The Agriculture Ministry specified that the leading regions by area sown with winter grain crops are: Mykolaiv region with 368,800 hectares, including 288,000 hectares of wheat and triticale, 79,300 hectares of barley and 1,500 hectares of rye; Dnipropetrovsk region with 284,600 hectares, including 262,100 hectares of wheat and triticale, 21,200 hectares of barley and 1,300 hectares of rye; and Poltava region with 200,100 hectares, including 191,900 hectares of wheat and triticale, 3,200 hectares of barley and 5,000 hectares of rye.</p>
<hr/><p>08.10.2026 11:17 Ділові новини, Головнi новини, Фармацевтика та медицина</p><h3>Внаслідок удару по Краматорську загинуло 12 людей – ОВА</h3><p class=MsoNormal>Київ. 8 жовтня. ІНТЕРФАКС-УКРАЇНА – Російські окупанти завдали удару по Краматорську, повідомляє очільник Донецької обласної військової адміністрації Вадим Філашкін.</p>
